"s1.text": "Five mascots thrown into worlds too big for them. For the first time, characters condemned to smile are allowed to be afraid, to doubt, to get lost.",
"s2.text": "A stay in Kyoto and then Rishikesh led her to the Japanese Godai and the Vedic Pañca Bhūta. Each colour joins a primordial element.",
"home.kicker": "Two series · ten works",
"home.lead": "Candice Shell is a former American art director who now paints the mascots she spent fifteen years selling.",
"home.practice": "The practice",
"home.practice.text": "She paints in oil on canvas, after dozens of pencil sketches of each character, a habit left over from the mascot model sheets of her old job. Her canvases are signed on the back, then released as limited-edition prints on aluminium.",
"panel.smile": "Smile content",
"panel.r1": "Drawn, 2004–2019",
"panel.r1v": "about 40,000",
