"panel.r3": "Ordered since",
"panel.note": "None of the first 40,000 was allowed to hesitate.",
"home.all": "All ten works",
"home.artist": "The artist",
"home.artist.q": "“They're the only smiles nobody ordered from me.”",
"home.artist.text": "Born in Ohio in 1978, the daughter of a food flavour chemist. Fifteen years in candy and cereal packaging in Chicago. She now lives in Madrid, in the Lavapiés neighbourhood.",
"home.artist.cta": "Full biography",
"home.corr": "Each colour appears in both series. Five diptychs, read side by side.",
"q1": "I spent fifteen years drawing them a smile. The least I owed them was a fear.",
"q2": "A logo is a face that has been forbidden to doubt.",
"q3": "Everyone has a shell. I paint what melts underneath.",
"q4": "I sign on the back. I spent my life putting names on the front of things.",
"q5": "The desert was me. So was the lasso.",
"q6": "I went to India to find myself. I found five elements and a sugar-free diet.",
"q7": "I don't explain my work. The gallery does that very well, and far too much.",
"col.yellow": "Yellow",
